// Spot weld: the laser does not move.
//
// Every other case in this repo interpolates (250 -> 340) um over 2.5 ms, i.e.
// 36 mm/s. That scan is the reason the radial distributions here could not be
// compared with the ESRF data, which is spot welds about a STATIC axis, and it
// is why radialSeeding carries an axisVelocity at all.
//
// The block grading already puts the fine cells at the domain centre, so a
// stationary source at x = 250 um sits in the refined region for the whole run
// rather than scanning out of it.
(
    (0         (250e-6 700e-6 250e-6))
    (2.5e-3    (250e-6 700e-6 250e-6))
)
